<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-5195] Java version check in common.sh checks wrong java</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-5195</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;tt&gt;check_java_version&lt;/tt&gt; function in bin/common.sh ignores JAVA_HOME and checks the default &lt;tt&gt;java&lt;/tt&gt; command in PATH, which may not be the version used by Zeppelin and interpreters.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&lt;p&gt;CentOS 7.6&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;default java is 1.8.0_60&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;zeppelin-env.sh contains JAVA_HOME pointing to openjdk 1.8.0_275&lt;/p&gt;</environment>
